# Authentication note: data requests require Wida session/antiforgery cookies.
# Mutations also require X-CSRF-TOKEN from GET /api/auth/session.
# Use the signed-in frontend for the interactive flow; see docs/authentication.md.
# Run requests individually after following README.md.
# Replace the IDs with values returned by your own requests.
# The all-zero GUIDs below are placeholders, not seeded records.
@wida_api_HostAddress = https://localhost:7127
@documentId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@invoiceId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@processingRunId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### List documents
GET {{wida_api_HostAddress}}/api/documents
Accept: application/json

### Upload a document
# Replace the path below with an existing local file before sending.
# Multipart file inclusion requires an HTTP client that supports the '< path' syntax.
POST {{wida_api_HostAddress}}/api/documents
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WidaDocumentBoundary

--WidaDocumentBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="invoice.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< /absolute/path/invoice.pdf
--WidaDocumentBoundary--

### Get document metadata (copy the upload response id into documentId)
GET {{wida_api_HostAddress}}/api/documents/{{documentId}}
Accept: application/json

### Create an invoice (only one invoice per document)
POST {{wida_api_HostAddress}}/api/invoices
Accept: application/json
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "documentId": "{{documentId}}",
  "supplierName": "Example Supplier",
  "invoiceNumber": "INV-001",
  "invoiceDate": "2026-09-06",
  "dueDate": "2026-10-06",
  "currency": "USD",
  "subtotalAmount": 100,
  "taxAmount": 10,
  "totalAmount": 110,
  "lines": [
    {
      "lineNumber": 1,
      "description": "Example item",
      "quantity": 2,
      "unitPrice": 50,
      "lineAmount": 100
    }
  ]
}

### Get an invoice (copy the invoice creation response id into invoiceId)
GET {{wida_api_HostAddress}}/api/invoices/{{invoiceId}}
Accept: application/json

### Get the invoice attached to a document
GET {{wida_api_HostAddress}}/api/invoices/document/{{documentId}}
Accept: application/json

### Create a manual Pending run (does not start analysis; no Azure settings required)
POST {{wida_api_HostAddress}}/api/processing/documents/{{documentId}}
Accept: application/json

### Analyze an invoice with Azure Document Intelligence
# Sends the stored document to Azure and waits for analysis during the request.
# Creates a new run. Inspect status even on HTTP 201: it can be Failed.
# Requires Azure endpoint/key. Results include extractedFields and review flags.
POST {{wida_api_HostAddress}}/api/processing/documents/{{documentId}}/invoice
Accept: application/json

### Get a processing run and extracted fields (copy a response id into processingRunId)
GET {{wida_api_HostAddress}}/api/processing/{{processingRunId}}
Accept: application/json

### List processing runs for a document
GET {{wida_api_HostAddress}}/api/processing/documents/{{documentId}}
Accept: application/json
